WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:01.545
The numbers are wrong.

2
00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:03.605
And now it is your problem.

3
00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:05.555
Even when another team caused it.

4
00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:08.715
At senior level, you own the trust in the data.

5
00:00:08.735 --> 00:00:14.540
Three steps: prevent with contracts, detect with tests, and recover from incidents.

6
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.700
First: prevent bad data.

7
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.513
A data contract is a promise from the producer.

8
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.510
These columns, these types, this freshness.

9
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.622
To add an optional column is safe.

10
00:00:24.642 --> 00:00:27.820
To rename or remove one breaks consumers.

11
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.770
So a breaking change gets a new version, and a warning to the consumers.

12
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.430
Second: detect it before users do.

13
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.342
Write the new data to a staging place.

14
00:00:37.362 --> 00:00:38.580
Audit it with checks.

15
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.640
Publish only if they pass.

16
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.915
So bad data never reaches a dashboard.

17
00:00:42.935 --> 00:00:46.090
The old, good data stays in place.

18
00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.600
Third: what does healthy data mean?

19
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.360
Watch four things: freshness, volume, schema, and the values themselves.

20
00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.385
Then set a target that users feel.

21
00:00:55.405 --> 00:01:00.485
For example: ready by seven, on 99 days of 100.

22
00:01:00.505 --> 00:01:03.095
Last: the bad data is already out.

23
00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:04.170
First contain it.

24
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.270
Then fix the cause.

25
00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.270
Then backfill.

26
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.355
Then write down what you learned.

27
00:01:08.375 --> 00:01:09.705
Tell the users early.

28
00:01:09.725 --> 00:01:12.830
Silence costs more trust than the bug.

29
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.115
Quick recap of data quality.

30
00:01:15.135 --> 00:01:16.540
Contracts prevent.

31
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.640
Write, audit, publish detects.

32
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.250
And contain an incident before you fix it.

33
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.370
Now start the first lesson below.
